{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7xor3JNr8VBNr7F3Jeu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I withdrew the record for span `u4` as an `atom` gap instead of revising it. The law is now blocked until the operator decides the gap.\n\n**Why:** `u4` is a condition span. With the words it borrows from `u5`, it means the approaching vehicle is using \"at least one flashing red warning lamp visible from the front.\" The `sig.warning_lamp` atom lists a facing attribute, but Core's formula forms only take `[track, colour]` or `[track, colour, mode]`. So no rule can say \"facing front.\"\n\n**Why not drop the facing:** a red flashing lamp facing any direction is a weaker condition. The duty would then arise when a vehicle closes from behind showing only rear- or side-facing red flashers, which the law doesn't cover. Rule 3/3b doesn't allow narrowing a condition span that way. No other atom can stand in for it: `rel.visible` explicitly says it is not a lamp being lit, and `rel.bearing` gives a road user's position, not which way a lamp faces.\n\n**What would unblock it:** a Core form `sig_warning_lamp [track, colour, mode, facing]`. Per the coder's note, the rule would then only need `.lit \"front\"` added to the lamp atom and the `no_atom` narrowing removed. Every witness already builds its lamps facing front.\n\n**Separate issue (not part of this withdrawal):** the coder also flagged that the reading puts no road-user class in the authorized-emergency-vehicle aggregate. The `u2` limb (authorized emergency vehicle) can then never be true, so a scene with an ambulance or fire truck comes out unknown. Every decided witness therefore uses the regulatory-agency limb. That needs fixing in the reading, outside this node.\n\nThe output is `record.jsonl` in the repair directory."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2247,"cache_read_input_tokens":82071,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2247},"output_tokens":594,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"us","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d4abaee2-3453-4e57-8792-63957500d3e9","uuid":"ae2e1fe3-d0e2-45fc-a0ff-5980a7f201cc","timestamp":"2026-11-17T05:39:50.956Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7xoqXXxzapUzsRXgtXL"}
